# Static Website Hosting using Ubuntu + Nginx

This is a cleaner and more professional method for your CC practical.

You will:

✅ Launch Ubuntu Server
✅ Install Nginx
✅ Host Static Website
✅ Access Website using Public IP

---

# Step 1 — Launch EC2 Ubuntu Instance

Go to:

```text id="wz7evn"
AWS Console
→ EC2
→ Launch Instance
```

---

# Configure Instance

## Name

```text id="e7b2tw"
nginx-static-server
```

---

## AMI

Select:

```text id="el6v9q"
Ubuntu Server 22.04 LTS
```

---

## Instance Type

```text id="5q0jz4"
t2.micro
```

---

## Key Pair

Create/download `.pem` file.

---

# Step 2 — Configure Security Group

Allow these ports:

| Type  | Port |
| ----- | ---- |
| SSH   | 22   |
| HTTP  | 80   |
| HTTPS | 443  |

---

# Step 3 — Launch Instance

Click:

```text id="i2npaf"
Launch Instance
```

---

# Step 4 — Connect to Ubuntu Server

Copy Public IP.

Example:

```text id="77j7nx"
13.233.XX.XX
```

---

# SSH Connection

## Windows PowerShell

```bash id="2ey3j8"
ssh -i mykey.pem ubuntu@YOUR_PUBLIC_IP
```

Example:

```bash id="1bupx7"
ssh -i awskey.pem ubuntu@13.233.XX.XX
```

---

# Step 5 — Update Ubuntu

```bash id="55a0d4"
sudo apt update
```

---

# Step 6 — Install Nginx

```bash id="3vw5g7"
sudo apt install nginx -y
```

---

# Step 7 — Start Nginx

```bash id="0v7z9t"
sudo systemctl start nginx
```

Enable on boot:

```bash id="1l3e5j"
sudo systemctl enable nginx
```

---

# Step 8 — Check Nginx Status

```bash id="71obco"
sudo systemctl status nginx
```

You should see:

```text id="ukuvph"
active (running)
```

Press:

```text id="d65uw8"
Q
```

to exit.

---

# Step 9 — Open Website Directory

```bash id="mrj5u1"
cd /var/www/html
```

---

# Step 10 — Remove Default Page

```bash id="4a1crz"
sudo rm index.nginx-debian.html
```

---

# Step 11 — Create Static Website

```bash id="n6qws8"
sudo nano index.html
```

Paste:

```html id="vuv2vp"
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>

<head>
    <title>Cloud Computing Assignment</title>
</head>

<body>

    <h1>Static Website Hosted using Nginx</h1>

    <h2>Ubuntu Cloud Server</h2>

    <p>Name: Vivek Falke</p>

    <p>Cloud Computing Practical</p>

</body>

</html>
```

---

# Save File

```text id="w6ff0w"
CTRL + X
Y
ENTER
```

---

# Step 12 — Restart Nginx

```bash id="b38g18"
sudo systemctl restart nginx
```

---

# Step 13 — Open Website

Browser:

```text id="s7sz3s"
http://YOUR_PUBLIC_IP
```

Example:

```text id="7x37od"
http://13.233.XX.XX
```

Your static website will open publicly.

